Z||000000||Monkeyman||02-11-2001||10:44 PM||||I want one.  Only problem is that I have limited cash + the Grape Ape.  Anyone have a nice V65 Magna for sale?  Interesting trades (GA + cash)??<P>For those of you that are unfamiliar with the bike, it was one of the most powerful bikes in the mid '80s.  Cruiser style, with lots of high tech features.  The styling was way ahead of it's time, too.  It doesn't have that mid '80s look to it.  Still looks modern, even today.  If anyone's interested, I'll post a pic of one once I get around to downloading PIP.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||02-11-2001||10:54 PM||||That bike is awesome. My dad had a blue one when they first came out ('83 or '84 I think) but he had to sell it after I was born.  He still talks about that bike, he has a picture of it on his desk. <P>For the heck of it I searched auto trader and there was one with 11k miles for 3800 obo.  Sounds like a good deal <BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-11-2001||10:59 PM||||Thanx, but $3800 is too much for one unless it's pristine and has a bunch of options (backrest/6 pack rack, case guard, etc) that I don't want anyway.  I appreciate the info, though.  I'm hopeing that there will be a forum member in need of a decent '85 GT that wants to do some partial trading.  I still have to put part of the interior back together before I can snap some pics of the Grape Ape to post on eBay.||||reg||1
Z||000003||WampusCat||02-11-2001||11:25 PM||||I had an '84 V65 for a while.  It was a lot of fun to play around town on.  Tons of torque but it handled like a truck compared to a modern sportbike.  I didn't like it for long trips because the straight upright seating made my torso act like a drag chute and it made my arms tired holding against the wind.  I later got a VFR750 and liked that much better, no problems doing 500 mile days.  The V65 did put a big grin on my face whenever I twisted that throttle tho.  I paid $1800 for mine in '91, sold it for $1600 in '93||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||02-12-2001||10:11 AM||||WampusCat,<BR>I'm guessing that your V 65 was a Sabre.<BR>I used to have one, too. Just like you described, it was a rocketship, but was one of the most evil handling bikes I have ever ridden. Only street bike that I have ever gotten "sideways" (but <I>that</I> was my fault). Took several weeks for the pinch marks to wear out of the seat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <BR>I've known folks who had the V 65 Magna, and didn't have any complaints about the handling.<BR>Good luck with your search, Monkeyman.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
